refactor(LabelLayer): apply architecture node and simplify process.

* LabelLayer extends GeometryLayer;
* Introduce DomNode and LabelsNode to structure data in Node architecture;
* simplify and optimize the process post-convert and the label culling;

## motivation

* remove last object in TileMesh;
* will simplify removal ObjectReemovalHelper;

refactor(test): robustify test-example target

The exampleCanRenderTest was a bit misnamed and could lead to strange results
since it waited for the LAYERS_INITIALIZED event, which is only fired when
layers are added...

Also all tests duplicated the same boilerplate code:

    page.setViewport({ width: 400, height: 300 });
    await page.goto(`http://localhost:${itownsPort}/examples/3dtiles.html`);
    await page.waitFor('#viewerDiv > canvas');
    const result = await exampleCanRenderTest(page, this.test.fullTitle());

Two new functions have been added, and exampleCanRenderTest has been removed:
    loadExample: is equivalent to the above code
    waitUntilItownsIsIdle: is to be used when something has been changed in the
view and we want to wait until itowns has finished working.

refactoring(core): remove Layer.parsingOptions.

Layer.parsingOptions are removed.

Parser options parameter, with crsOut and crsIn, are deprecated.
Use new parsing options, '{ in, out }' Object, instead of.

New parsing options construction:

parsing options will have two properties in and out
* 'in' will be data specification for in data.
* 'out' will be data specification for out feature.

'in' and 'out' could be set, respectively, by 'Source' and 'Layer'.

// custom parsing  option to convert 'EPSG:4326' data to 'EPSG:4978' `Feature`.
const parsingOptions = {
   in: { crs: 'EPSG:4326'  },
   out: { crs: 'EPSG:4978'  },
};
// For a layer the options will be
const parsingOptionsForLayer = {
   in: layer.source,
   out: layer,
};

